e incentive , making the model less likely to study such expressions. Consequently, there exists a trade off: for a given expression/strategy, if it is both correct, useful and generalized (e.g. brute computation), the model would be very much willing to learn it; on the contrary, if a given expression/strategy is correct, but hard and field-specific. The model would tend to give up on this expression/strategy, and in turn pay more attention to more friendly expressions or strategies.

